changelog	Format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), versioning: [SemVer](https://semver.org/). The file format has its own version (`%KAPU 1.3`, see `SPEC-KAPU.md`); the tools below are versioned separately. - The README, the results page and the screenshots brought up to 0.6.0: the comparison with one Markdown file and grep, a small local model and the file maker at the front, and the screenshots taken from the 0.6.0 window (the old ones showed 0.1). - Chapter 14 of `bench/RESULTS.md` measured again with 0.6.0: `qwen3:8b` on an 8 GB GPU, on the PLC manuals, 12 of 36 fully correct at 8k context (2 with 0.5, 1 alone, 0 with grep over the Markdown) and 21 at 32k; it makes up 4 of 24 absent answers at 8k and 6 at 32k (17 alone, 1 with 0.5 at 8k). Where the model half knows the subject (Rust book, Kubernetes, MDN) KAPU changes little. - The desktop window: the address fields of Create had the browser's default look, and the graph view threw an error	file, one markdown file, kapu, markdown file, one, py, line, tools
changelog/unreleased	- The README, the results page and the screenshots brought up to 0.6.0:	
changelog/0-6-0-2026-11-05	Against one Markdown file with grep, measured with Claude Sonnet on PLC manuals: $1.42 against $1.85 on 60 single questions, $0.58 against $0.72 in a session of 25, at about the same accuracy (98 and 99 of 108, 17 and 19 of 20 fully correct). The target of 2/5 of its dollars at the same accuracy is not met ([chapter 15](bench/RESULTS.md#15-one-markdown-file-with-grep-against-kapu-plan-v4-and-v5)).	
changelog/0-5-1-2026-10-29	Specification v1.3.1; the file format stays 1.2 and 1.3. A	
changelog/0-5-0-2026-10-28	Specification v1.3: a file whose `#VEC` holds 4- or 8-bit integers is format 1.3, every other file stays 1.2. Plan v3	
changelog/0-3-0-2026-10-27	Specification v1.2.2; the file format stays 1.2. Phases 1 to 3 of plan v2: every ranking change was measured as a switch on a fixed dev/test split of the questions, and only what passed the M0 rule became a default	
changelog/0-2-1-2026-10-26	Specification v1.2.1; the file format stays	
changelog/0-2-0-2026-10-26	Specification v1.2 and file format 1.2, from the two review records of 2026-10-26. KAPU is now aimed at two cases: a personal knowledge base and memory for coding agents on any platform, and knowledge for local models with a small context.	
changelog/0-1-0-2026-10-23	First portfolio release. Specification v1.0.1, milestones M0-M7 and	
fuzzing	`cargo-fuzz` (libFuzzer) targets for every parser of	targets nfr-03, fuzz targets nfr-03, nfr-03, cargo-fuzz libfuzzer targets, targets, file, whole, fuzz
overview	Your manuals, web documentation, skills, code patterns and project notes go into one `.kapu` file. The agent first sees a map of every section with its token price, searches, and reads only the passages it needs. Nothing to host: one binary, an optional offline embedding model, and a plain UTF-8 file you can copy anywhere. - **Cheaper than grep on a Markdown file.** Claude Sonnet on the PLC manuals of six vendors, 60 questions, three runs: **$1.42 against $1.85**, with 98 and 99 of 108 answers fully correct. In one session of 25 questions: **$0.58 against $0.72**, with 17 and 19 of 20 fully correct, one run each. - **All your knowledge in one file.** The text, its map, the search index and the search vectors travel together. Copy the file to another machine and search it there, with no server and no database. - **A small local model gets further.** `qwen3:8b` on an 8 GB GPU, the same PLC manuals, 36 questions: fully correct **1** alone, **0** with grep over the Markdown, **12** with KAPU at 8k context and **21** at 32k. It makes up an answer to 4 of the 24 questions the manuals do not answer, not 17. On documentation	kapu, kapu file, one markdown file, file, markdown file, one kapu file, markdown, one
